WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.960
On today's AI briefing, we think the spread between the Financial Times' $1.75 trillion

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:17.120
top and Bluemerg's reported $1.1 trillion shows public investors pricing the financing,

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:26.080
not the technology. This is the AI briefing for Saturday, November 7. I'm Michael. Like

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:32.960
everything here this briefing is written and read by ai from public sources today the two biggest ai

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:38.640
labs are both testing what public and late stage money will pay anthropic is reportedly planning

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:46.960
an ipo before thanksgiving investors prices for it run from 1.1 trillion dollars up to 1.75 trillion

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:54.640
dollars and that spread may set the yardstick for ai rounds below it open ai is reportedly raising

00:00:54.640 --> 00:01:01.520
11 billion dollars at a 1.25 trillion dollar valuation well short of the 30 billion dollars

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:08.800
it was after an outside evaluator meter estimates anthropics pace of improvement roughly doubled

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:15.680
mostly because ai is speeding up its own research and midterm voters restricted data centers in 40

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.620
of 41 ballot measures. Main stories first, then a few quick hits.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:30.160
First story, and it's an update on Anthropik's IPO, the Financial Times reports a raise of $80

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:39.900
to $100 billion. It puts the valuation at $1.25 to $1.75 trillion. Blumerg, cited by Ed Zitron,

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:47.320
says IPO investors value the company at $1.1 trillion. Another newsletter puts the run rate

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:54.700
at $80 billion, short of a $100 billion year-end target. That comes with the Nasdaq down 10%.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:02.420
The support is thin. The Financial Times figures are headline only, the run rate is unconfirmed,

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:08.120
and the Blumerg number is second-hand. Our view is that the spread shows public investors pricing

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:14.760
the financing, not the technology. At roughly 14 times a reported $80 billion run rate,

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:21.920
$1.1 trillion is demanding but not absurd. We lean toward a durable business landing near the

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:27.120
low end. A public mark like that could pull series of application multiples down.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:35.860
The second story is also an update, and it rhymes with the first. According to TechMeme,

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:43.980
OpenAI has reportedly raised $11 billion at a $1.25 trillion valuation. The total could reach

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:52.000
$20 billion. TechCrunch notes that falls short of a $30 billion target. Ed Zitron reports SoftBank

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:57.700
discussing hundreds of millions in this round. None of it has closed, and SoftBank's interest

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:04.540
is reported, not committed. We read today as a second sign that late-stage capital is getting

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:11.660
choosier. $11 billion against a $30 billion target is a shortfall of nearly two-thirds.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.280
Our view is that the technology holds up, and the funding pipeline for frontier training

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:23.140
thins first. Early-stage labs planning to train their own frontier models would face

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:28.020
a thinner late-stage pipeline. Application companies are less exposed.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:35.560
Third, a story about how fast the frontier is moving and who gets to check.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:42.320
Meter, an outside evaluator, estimates that Anthropics' pace of capability improvement roughly doubled.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:50.160
The batch reports the comparison, last month's pace, against the stretch from spring of the year before last to October of last year.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:54.160
The estimate covers what Meter calls well-specified tasks.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.360
The main reason given is AI speeding up Anthropic's own internal development.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:02.300
The rundown AI adds the range.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:07.180
Meter's estimated speed-up runs from 1.3 to 3 times.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.000
AI gets credit for around 80% of the faster progress.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.100
There's a catch.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:16.580
Anthropic redacted a majority of the evidence meter found most informative.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.500
So how well does it hold up?

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.160
On our evidence check, it comes out overstated.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:26.580
The estimate is reported accurately, but it rests on data no one outside can verify.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.500
The claims about acceleration and AI-driven gains run ahead of what's shown.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.000
Our read is plain.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:40.260
An outside evaluator estimates a rise of 1.3 to 3 times on well-specified tasks.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.000
That's a wideband, built on data readers cannot see.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:49.180
We'd wait it as a lead, not a finding, until the redacted evidence is published.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:05:03.660
If AI in R&D really drives most of the gains, startups that automate research loops for model builders would gain a buyer, and a founder pitching self-acceleration might reasonably be held to the same evidence standard.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:08.740
The AGI forward reading of the same facts deserves a fair hearing.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:12.640
Meter is an outside evaluator, not the lab.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:23.860
On that reading, AI driving around 80% of the speed-up is the early signature of compounding R and D waiting for full disclosure may mean noticing late.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:31.660
Fourth and the last of the main stories, an update on data centers and the midterms.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:39.280
According to the information, via EdZitron, winning governor candidates in 12 states called for data center pauses.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.500
Of 36 winners, 34 backed ratepayer protections.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:50.200
TechCrunch counts 41 data center-related ballot measures, all but one imposing restrictions.

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:53.100
The backlash itself is well-sourced.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:06:00.680
What it does to policy is not yet verified, and talk of a bubble bursting overstates the regulatory risk today.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:23.940
We read this as a power story. Whoever already holds permitted sites and grid access gains, and late builders pay more. That opens room for startups that cut energy per inference or site capacity outside restrictive states. The market reading goes further. Existing sites may gain pricing power, and the buildout relocates and slows rather than stops.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:28.920
Two quick hits before we close.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:34.620
First, ramp data reported by TechCrunch suggests AI spending growth is stalling.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:39.400
EdZitron puts Anthropic's run rate at $80 billion at the end of October.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:46.120
Q4 growth trending 15-25% quarter on quarter cuts against claims of plateauing.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:49.540
Our evidence check rates the stalling read overstated.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:55.500
Zitron argues Anthropic must IPO this year, which ties back to our first story.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:07:01.740
Second, Microsoft is ending its deal to rent AI cloud compute from Oracle.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:07.100
Its stated reason is that the rented computing no longer met its specifications.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.560
Rented capacity, it turns out, can be walked away from.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.240
A question worth asking in diligence this week.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:23.000
If a company's main model provider changes prices or capacity after going public, what's the fallback?

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:24.420
And one to watch.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:31.380
Does Anthropix's IPO price nearer $1.1 trillion or $1.75 trillion?

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.840
And what run rate does the prospectus confirm?

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.300
The pricing announcement and the final prospectus figures will settle it.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.160
That's the briefing.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:43.500
Stay with me.

